quran[7]{c,v,t}:
  3,23,"Have you not seen those given a portion of the Book being called to Allah’s Book that it might judge between them, then a group of them turn away (refusing to comply)? And they are disregardful."
  3,24,That is because they say: ‘The Fire shall not touch us except for a (small) number of days. They have been deceived in their religion by the lies they used to fabricate.
  3,25,"But how (horrible) will it be when we gather them on a Day about which there is no doubt, when every soul shall be paid in full for what it has earned, and they will not be wronged?"
  3,26,"Say: ‘O Allah, Master of the kingdom! You give authority to whomever You will, and You take away authority from whomever You will. You honour whomever You will, and You disgrace whomever You will. All good is in Your Hand. Indeed, You are All-Capable of everything."
  3,27,"You merge the night into the day, and You merge the day into the night. You bring the living out of the dead, and You bring the dead out of the living. And You provide sustenance to whomever You will without measure.’"
  3,28,"The believers should not take the disbelievers as guardians (or trustworthy protectors) instead of the believers. And whoever does that will get nothing from (the guardianship of) Allah unless you guard yourselves against them with full consciousness. Allah warns you to beware of (disobeying) Him, and to Allah is the eventual return."
  3,29,"Say: ‘Whether you conceal what is in your hearts or reveal it, Allah knows it, and He (thoroughly) knows whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth. And Allah is All-Capable of everything.’"
